      "mentions": 21,
      "title": {
        "en": "Skilled emergency team with service inconsistencies"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Numerous pet parents express gratitude for compassionate, calm emergency doctors and technicians who provide urgent interventions during life-threatening crises. However, several dissatisfied clients criticize front desk personnel, reporting perceived indifference, unprofessional behavior in waiting areas, and inadequate post-discharge follow-up."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "results",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 14,
      "title": {
        "en": "Effective stabilization during acute emergencies"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients credit the urgent care team with lifesaving medical treatments, highlighting rapid diagnosis, effective toxicity interventions, and thorough overnight patient monitoring. While most medical outcomes are praised, a few reviewers report disappointment regarding unresolved diagnostic answers and differing clinical opinions."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "waiting",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 11,
      "title": {
        "en": "Emergency triage leading to lobby delays"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Lobby waiting times depend heavily on the severity of incoming cases. While critically unstable pets are admitted immediately for triage, clients arriving with non-emergency concerns frequently report waiting two to three hours in the clinic, noting that wait estimates can shift as urgent cases arrive."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Does the hospital operate on a triage system?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, the facility prioritizes life-threatening cases immediately upon arrival, meaning non-critical ailments may experience extended waiting times."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Are pets monitored overnight during emergency hospitalizations?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Yes, clients report overnight medical monitoring and fluid therapies for animals recovering from severe trauma or acute illnesses."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "How are emergency costs and estimates handled?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Staff provide diagnostic estimates before admitting pets, though total costs for intensive emergency care and testing can accumulate quickly."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    }
  ],
